```mdl
verdict playEngineMove: Play plays a random legal move for the requested side and persists the PGN.
  status: untested
  evidence: [github:dxos/dxos/packages/plugins/plugin-chess/src/types/ChessOperation.ts#Play, github:dxos/dxos/packages/plugins/plugin-chess/src/operations/play.ts]
  walkthrough:
    - The operation declares a chess Game ref and optional side in, pgn and move out. github:dxos/dxos/packages/plugins/plugin-chess/src/types/ChessOperation.ts#Play
    - The handler replays the PGN, picks a random legal move if it is that side's turn, and writes PGN and FEN. github:dxos/dxos/packages/plugins/plugin-chess/src/operations/play.ts
  note: The key and shape match. The "engine" is a uniform random choice from `chess.moves()`. No test invokes it.
```

```mdl
verdict submitMove: The Move operation applies a SAN move to a Game ref and returns the PGN; it has no player or typed errors.
  status: diverged
  evidence: [github:dxos/dxos/packages/plugins/plugin-chess/src/types/ChessOperation.ts#Move, github:dxos/dxos/packages/plugins/plugin-chess/src/operations/move.ts]
  note: |
    Key `org.dxos.operation.chess.move` matches, but the input is `{ game: Ref, move: string }` and the output
    `{ pgn }`, not `{ game, player, move } → Game`. An illegal move throws chess.js's "Invalid move" before any
    write, so it is atomic; there is no player-turn check and no `WrongTurn`/`GameOver` error. Not tested.
```

